{ ============================================================
  ADAPTIVE FARMER - TREND BEARISH STRATEGY
  Signal Name : Trendbearish_V1
  MC Load Name: Trendbearish_V1
  Description : Trend Short - weekly SMA13 bear filter + Donchian30 breakdown
                + ZLEMA momentum. Short only.
  Version     : 5.3 + SetStopContract + SL_Pct (v5.2 base)
  Symbol      : TXF1 (Taiwan Stock Index Futures Front Month)
  Platform    : MultiCharts 9.0 PowerLanguage x64
  Timeframe   : 60-Minute (Day + Night Sessions, grid verified
                vs Excel timestamps: day 09:45-13:45, night
                16:00-05:00 hourly close stamps)

  CHANGELOG:
    5.1  Label unification (TS_ prefix). No logic changes.
    5.2  (2026-06-12) Holiday Flat Rule v3 + safety rails:
         - Iron Rule: flat (0 position) BEFORE the 05:00 close of
           the last night session preceding every market closure.
           Audit found 1 historical violation: short held across
           the 2025 Dragon Boat closure (-33,000, exited only
           after the gap via TS_StructureTP).
         - Holiday_Tail registry (63 dates, TAIFEX-verified, same
           registry as L1 V2.4+). Tail bars (00:00-05:00, stamped
           with the first closed date): entries blocked; forced
           BuyToCover from Holiday_Flat_Time (03:00 on the 60M
           grid -> fill 03:00, retry 04:00, flat before 05:00).
         - Registry_Valid_Until fail-safe: beyond the verified
           horizon block entries + flatten (TS_RegistryEnd) +
           30-day red chart warning.
         - Manual_Kill_Switch added (TS_Kill) for typhoon-class
           unscheduled closures.
         - Inserted as Priority 0 in the SECTION 13 exit chain
           (above TS_WeeklyExit). Entry gate added in SECTION 7.
         - Header performance reflects the OLD module set;
           re-backtest after deployment. Deploy only when flat
           (changes history for holiday-crossing trades).
    5.2+ (2026-06-18) P3b Immediate Stop Guard:
         - SetStopLoss = MC engine-level stop, active on entry
           bar (no IOG dependency). Closes the structural 60-min
           unprotected window between fill and first custom stop.
         - Distance = AbsValue((DC_Lower + ATR*SL_ATR_Ratio) -
           Close) * BigPointValue. Same anchor as Section 8 SL.
         - Called only when not short (MP>=0) -> freezes when
           short position opens (same principle as SL_Locked).
         - Does NOT replace Section 8-13 exit logic. Dormant
           backup once custom stops tighten.
         - Deploy only when flat.
    5.3  (2026-07-26) INITIAL STOP HARDENING (SetStopContract + SL_Pct):
         BUG FIX - SetStopContract MISSING (same issue as L4 v14.6, L5 v19.9):
           SetStopLoss without SetStopContract = stop dollar amount
           is for the TOTAL POSITION, not per contract.
           L2 trades 2 contracts -> engine stop was 2x tighter than
           designed. SetStopContract makes SetStopLoss PER-CONTRACT.
         NEW - SL_Pct Percentage Stop Cap (SHORT mirror of L1/L3/L4/L5):
           ATR can spike in volatile regimes, causing the ATR-based
           stop (DC_Lower + ATR*1.1) to exceed any reasonable risk budget.
           SL_Pct caps max stop distance as pct of entry price.
           For SHORT: ceiling = EntryPrice + EntryPrice * SL_Pct / 100.
           Applied to BOTH engine stop (P3b) and custom stop (Section 8).
           MC sweep 0.00-5.00 step 0.25: converge at SL_Pct=1.25.
           1.25 is tightest non-degrading value (rows 6-21 identical
           to baseline). Below 1.00 degrades significantly
           (0.25 = -50% net, stops binding too tight on ATR spikes).

  PERFORMANCE (Excel Report 2026/07/26, Initial Capital 1M, SL_Pct=1.25):
    Net Profit    : 2,882,400 TWD
    Profit Factor : 2.88
    Win Rate      : 42.31%
    MDD           : -484,400 (-14.99%)
    Total Trades  : 78
    Avg Trade     : 44,345 TWD
    Sharpe (ann.) : 0.847
    Sortino       : 1.233

    PERFORMANCE CAVEATS (added 2026-08-25 audit):
      - The source Excel is NOT in the repo. These numbers cannot be
        reproduced from anything under version control. Treat as
        UNVERIFIED until the report is archived alongside the .pla.
      - "Initial Capital 1M" contradicts CLAUDE.md, which fixes the
        account basis at 2,000,000 for percent and MDD-percent. Note
        also that -484,400 / 1,000,000 = -48.4%, not the -14.99%
        printed above. One of the three figures is wrong. UNRESOLVED
        - do not rely on the percentages until this is settled.
      - Contracts, slippage and backtest window are not stated here.
        CLAUDE.md standard is 2 contracts, 1,000 NTD per side per lot.

    STATUS (as of 2026-08-25):
      Last closed trade 2025-06-03. 443 days (14.6 months) with zero
      trades; 2026 year-to-date = 0 trades. Rule #13 (minimum two
      trades per month) heavily breached.
      Probable cause, INFERRED and NOT MEASURED: FilterOK requires the
      weekly close below SMA(13) while the index ran 21,000 -> 47,000.
      A short-only strategy idling through a bull regime is expected
      behaviour, but the duration warrants a review.
      Source: docs/research/L2_reentry_L28_check_20260824.md
  ============================================================ }


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 1 - INPUTS
  ============================================================ }

Inputs:
   { Weekly trend filter - one quarter = 13 weeks }
   WkSMA_Len            ( 13   ),

   { Entry: Donchian channel }
   DC_Len               ( 30   ),

   { Entry: ZLEMA - fixed by formula, do not optimize }
   ZLEMA_Len            ( 20   ),
   ZLEMA_Lag            ( 9    ),

   { ATR period - shared by all modules }
   ATR_Len              ( 21   ),

   { C0 breakout confirmation: Close < DC_Lower - ATR * filter }
   C0_ATR_Filter        ( 0.45 ),

   { Initial SL buffer: SL_Trig = DC_Lower + ATR * ratio }
   SL_ATR_Ratio         ( 1.1  ),

   { TSL activation }
   Accel_M              ( 0.5  ),
   NLow_N               ( 15   ),
   MinBars              ( 3    ),

   { TSL tracking }
   TSL_K                ( 9    ),
   TSL_M                ( 1.0  ),

   { Structure reversal take profit }
   TP_N                 ( 30   ),

   { Trailing take profit }
   TTP_MinAtr           ( 4.0  ),
   TTP_RebPct           ( 1.5  ),

   { Stop profit: activate when profit >= stopProfitPoints_Shrt }
   { Allow drawback up to profitReturnPrcnt_Shrt % of peak profit }
   stopProfitPoints_Shrt  ( 250 ),
   profitReturnPrcnt_Shrt ( 55  ),

   { Holiday Flat Rule v3 (Iron Rule 2026-06-12) }
   Holiday_Flat_Time      ( 300 ),     { 03:00 trigger on 60M grid -> fill 03:00, retry 04:00 }
   Registry_Valid_Until   ( 1270101 ), { verified holiday-registry horizon; bump each Q4 }
   Manual_Kill_Switch     ( False ),

   { Monthly Settlement Flat (2026-06-17 added)
     TXF1 settles every 3rd Wed of month at 13:30.
     Detection: DayOfWeek=3 AND DayOfMonth in [15,21].
     Flat at 12:30 (1hr buffer before 13:30 settlement). }
   Settlement_Flat_Time   ( 1230 ),

   { v5.3: SetStopContract + SL_Pct (2026-07-26) }
   SL_Pct                 ( 1.25 );    { Pct stop cap for SHORT. Ceiling = Entry + Entry*SL_Pct/100. MC sweep converge = 1.25. }


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 2 - VARIABLES
  ============================================================ }

Variables:
   { Session }
   IsDay                ( False ),
   IsNight              ( False ),

   { Weekly filter }
   WkBarCount           ( 0     ),
   WkSMASum             ( 0     ),
   IsNewWeek            ( False ),
   FilterOK             ( False ),

   { Indicators }
   CompPrice            ( 0     ),
   ZLEMA_Val            ( 0     ),
   EMA20_Val            ( 0     ),
   DC_Lower             ( 0     ),
   ATR_Val              ( 0     ),

   { Entry flags }
   C0                   ( False ),
   C_A                  ( False ),
   C_B                  ( False ),

   { Initial stop loss }
   SL_Line              ( 0     ),
   SL_Trig              ( 0     ),
   SL_Locked            ( False ),

   { TSL activation }
   Accel                ( False ),
   NLow                 ( False ),
   C1_Bar               ( False ),
   TSL_Armed            ( False ),

   { TSL tracking }
   New_TSL              ( 0     ),
   TSL_Line             ( 0     ),
   Active_TSL           ( 0     ),
   Active_SL            ( 0     ),

   { Trailing take profit }
   LowestClose          ( 0     ),
   WaveProfit           ( 0     ),
   MinProfitPts         ( 0     ),
   TTP_Line             ( 0     ),
   TTP_Gate             ( False ),
   TTP_Fire             ( False ),

   { Stop profit }
   posbleProfit_Short   ( 0     ),
   stopProfitPrice      ( 0     ),

   { Loop counter and exit control }
   LoopIdx              ( 0     ),
   ExitFired            ( 0     ),

   { Holiday Flat Rule v3 }
   v_Holiday_Block      ( False ),
   v_Registry_Expired   ( False ),
   Registry_Warn_ID     ( -1    ),
   hidx                 ( 0     ),

   { Monthly Settlement Flat }
   v_Settlement_Day     ( False ),

   { v5.3 SL_Pct }
   v_Guard_Distance     ( 0 );


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 3 - ARRAYS
  WkCloses stores last WkSMA_Len completed weekly closes.
  Size 21 covers indices 0 to 20. Only indices 1 to 20 used.
  WkSMA_Len = 13, so indices 1 to 13 are actively used.
  ============================================================ }

Array: WkCloses[ 21 ] ( 0 ), Holiday_Tail[ 80 ] ( 0 );


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 4 - SESSION DETECTION
  IsDay   : 60M CLOSE stamps 09:45 to 12:45 (Time 945..1245).
            The 845 lower bound never binds - no bar carries a
            stamp in 845..944. NOTE the 13:45 day-session close
            bar is NOT included and falls into IsNight.
  IsNight : every other bar = night close stamps 16:00 to 05:00,
            PLUS the 13:45 day-session close bar.
  ============================================================ }

If ( Time >= 845 ) And ( Time <= 1245 ) Then
   IsDay = True
Else
   IsDay = False;

If IsDay = True Then
   IsNight = False
Else
   IsNight = True;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 4B - HOLIDAY FLAT RULE v3 (Iron Rule 2026-06-12)

  Holiday_Tail = last trading day + 1 calendar day = the date
  stamped on the 00:00-05:00 tail bars of the final night
  session before each market closure.

  Tail bars: block new entries; force BuyToCover from
  Holiday_Flat_Time (60M grid: trigger on the 03:00 bar, fill
  03:00, retry 04:00, always flat before the 05:00 close).
  Beyond Registry_Valid_Until the strategy fails safe.

  Dates: TAIFEX official calendars. 2026 verified 2026-06-12.
  Entries marked * reconstructed (Labor Days; 2025 new
  statutory holidays) - verify vs archived TAIFEX PDFs before
  trusting re-backtest stats on those windows.
  ============================================================ }

If CurrentBar = 1 Then Begin

   { --- 2019 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[1]  = 1190913;
   Holiday_Tail[2]  = 1191010;
   Holiday_Tail[3]  = 1200101;

   { --- 2020 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[4]  = 1200121;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[5]  = 1200228;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[6]  = 1200402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[7]  = 1200501;  { * Labor Day }
   Holiday_Tail[8]  = 1200625;  { Dragon Boat }
   Holiday_Tail[9]  = 1201001;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[10] = 1201009;  { National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[11] = 1210101;  { 2021 New Year }

   { --- 2021 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[12] = 1210206;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[13] = 1210227;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[14] = 1210402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[15] = 1210612;  { Dragon Boat }
   Holiday_Tail[16] = 1210918;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[17] = 1211009;  { National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[18] = 1211231;  { 2022 New Year }

   { --- 2022 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[19] = 1220127;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[20] = 1220226;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[21] = 1220402;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[22] = 1220430;  { * Labor Day (5/2 make-up) }
   Holiday_Tail[23] = 1220603;  { Dragon Boat }
   Holiday_Tail[24] = 1220909;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[25] = 1221008;  { National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[26] = 1221231;  { 2023 New Year }

   { --- 2023 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[27] = 1230118;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[28] = 1230225;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[29] = 1230401;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[30] = 1230429;  { * Labor Day }
   Holiday_Tail[31] = 1230622;  { Dragon Boat }
   Holiday_Tail[32] = 1230929;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[33] = 1231007;  { National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[34] = 1231230;  { 2024 New Year }

   { --- 2024 --- }
   Holiday_Tail[35] = 1240206;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[36] = 1240228;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[37] = 1240404;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[38] = 1240501;  { * Labor Day }
   Holiday_Tail[39] = 1240608;  { Dragon Boat }
   Holiday_Tail[40] = 1240917;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[41] = 1241010;  { National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[42] = 1250101;  { 2025 New Year }

   { --- 2025 (* rows pending check vs 114-yr TAIFEX PDF) --- }
   Holiday_Tail[43] = 1250123;  { CNY }
   Holiday_Tail[44] = 1250228;  { 228 }
   Holiday_Tail[45] = 1250403;  { Tomb Sweeping }
   Holiday_Tail[46] = 1250501;  { * Labor Day }
   Holiday_Tail[47] = 1250530;  { Dragon Boat (5/30 make-up) }
   Holiday_Tail[48] = 1250927;  { * Teachers Day (9/29 make-up) }
   Holiday_Tail[49] = 1251004;  { Mid-Autumn }
   Holiday_Tail[50] = 1251010;  { * National Day }
   Holiday_Tail[51] = 1251024;  { * Retrocession Day (10/24 make-up) }
   Holiday_Tail[52] = 1251225;  { * Constitution Day }
   Holiday_Tail[53] = 1260101;  { 2026 New Year }

   { --- 2026 (verified: TAIFEX official 115-yr calendar) --- }
   Holiday_Tail[54] = 1260212;  { CNY: final trading day 2/11 }
   Holiday_Tail[55] = 1260227;  { 228: 2/27 make-up, eve 2/26 }
   Holiday_Tail[56] = 1260403;  { Children/Tomb 4/3-4/6, eve 4/2 }
   Holiday_Tail[57] = 1260501;  { Labor Day 5/1-5/3, eve 4/30 }
   Holiday_Tail[58] = 1260619;  { Dragon Boat 6/19-6/21, eve 6/18 }
   Holiday_Tail[59] = 1260925;  { Mid-Autumn + Teachers 9/25-9/28, eve 9/24 }
   Holiday_Tail[60] = 1261009;  { National Day 10/9-10/11, eve 10/8 }
   Holiday_Tail[61] = 1261024;  { Retrocession 10/24-10/26, eve 10/23 }
   Holiday_Tail[62] = 1261225;  { Constitution 12/25-12/27, eve 12/24 }
   Holiday_Tail[63] = 1270101;  { 2027 New Year 1/1-1/3, eve 12/31 }

   { 2027 CNY onward: rebuild from TAIFEX 116-yr calendar in Q4 2026 }

End;

v_Holiday_Block = False;

If Time <= 500 Then Begin
   For hidx = 1 To 80 Begin
      If Date = Holiday_Tail[ hidx ] Then
         v_Holiday_Block = True;
   End;
End;

v_Registry_Expired = False;

If Date > Registry_Valid_Until Then Begin
   v_Registry_Expired = True;
   v_Holiday_Block    = True;
End;

{ Monthly Settlement Day detection (3rd Wed) }
v_Settlement_Day = ( DayOfWeek( Date ) = 3 ) and
                   ( DayOfMonth( Date ) >= 15 ) and
                   ( DayOfMonth( Date ) <= 21 );

If LastBarOnChart And
   DateToJulian( Date ) >= DateToJulian( Registry_Valid_Until ) - 30 Then Begin
   If Registry_Warn_ID < 0 Then Begin
      Registry_Warn_ID = Text_New( Date, Time, High + 400,
         "HOLIDAY REGISTRY EXPIRES " +
         NumToStr( Registry_Valid_Until, 0 ) +
         " - REBUILD FROM TAIFEX CALENDAR" );
      Text_SetColor( Registry_Warn_ID, Red );
      Text_SetSize( Registry_Warn_ID, 14 );
      Text_SetAttribute( Registry_Warn_ID, 1, True );
   End;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 5 - WEEKLY TREND FILTER

  FilterOK = True when prior completed weekly close is
  strictly below the 13-week (one quarter) SMA.

  Definition: weekly period = Friday 15:00 open to
  Friday 13:45 close. IsNewWeek fires when the prior bar
  is the Friday 12:45 bar (last completed day session bar).

  WkSMA_Len = 13 represents one full calendar quarter.
  FilterOK = True means the market has been below its
  quarterly average, confirming a bearish environment.
  ============================================================ }

If ( Time[1] = 1245 ) And
   ( DayOfWeek( Date[1] ) = 5 ) Then
   IsNewWeek = True
Else
   IsNewWeek = False;

If IsNewWeek = True Then Begin

   { STEP 1 - Shift array rightward }
   LoopIdx = WkSMA_Len;
   While LoopIdx > 1 Begin
      WkCloses[ LoopIdx ] = WkCloses[ LoopIdx - 1 ];
      LoopIdx = LoopIdx - 1;
   End;

   { STEP 2 - Insert just-completed week close at index 1 }
   WkCloses[1] = Close[1];

   { STEP 3 - Increment stored week count }
   If WkBarCount < WkSMA_Len Then
      WkBarCount = WkBarCount + 1;

   { STEP 4 - Recompute rolling SMA sum }
   WkSMASum = 0;
   LoopIdx  = 1;
   While LoopIdx <= WkBarCount Begin
      WkSMASum = WkSMASum + WkCloses[ LoopIdx ];
      LoopIdx  = LoopIdx + 1;
   End;

   { STEP 5 - Update FilterOK with warm-up guard }
   If WkBarCount >= WkSMA_Len Then Begin
      If WkCloses[1] < ( WkSMASum / WkSMA_Len ) Then
         FilterOK = True
      Else
         FilterOK = False;
   End Else
      FilterOK = False;

End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 6 - INDICATOR CALCULATIONS
  ============================================================ }

ATR_Val   = AvgTrueRange( ATR_Len );
DC_Lower  = Lowest( Low[1], DC_Len );
CompPrice = ( 2.0 * Close ) - Close[ ZLEMA_Lag ];
ZLEMA_Val = XAverage( CompPrice, ZLEMA_Len );
EMA20_Val = XAverage( Close, ZLEMA_Len );


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 7 - ENTRY CONDITIONS
  ============================================================ }

If Close < ( DC_Lower - ( ATR_Val * C0_ATR_Filter ) ) Then
   C0 = True
Else
   C0 = False;

If ZLEMA_Val < ZLEMA_Val[1] Then
   C_A = True
Else
   C_A = False;

If ZLEMA_Val < EMA20_Val Then
   C_B = True
Else
   C_B = False;

{ P3b: Immediate Stop Guard -- entry-bar protection (2026-06-18)
  SetStopLoss is MC engine-level: active on entry bar, no IOG dependency.
  Only called when not short -> freezes at signal-bar values once position opens.
  v5.3: SetStopContract makes SetStopLoss amount PER-CONTRACT (lot-invariant).
         SL_Pct caps engine stop distance as pct of Close.
    Close is used here because EntryPrice does not exist before the
    fill; the custom stop in Section 8 anchors on EntryPrice instead. }
If MarketPosition >= 0 Then Begin
   v_Guard_Distance = AbsValue( ( DC_Lower + ATR_Val * SL_ATR_Ratio ) - Close );
   If SL_Pct > 0 Then
      v_Guard_Distance = MinList( v_Guard_Distance, Close * SL_Pct / 100 );
   SetStopContract;
   SetStopLoss( v_Guard_Distance * BigPointValue );
End;

If FilterOK = True And
   C0       = True And
   C_A      = True And
   C_B      = True And
   ( v_Holiday_Block = False ) And
   ( v_Settlement_Day = False ) And
   ( MarketPosition = 0 ) Then
   SellShort( "TS_Entry" ) Next Bar at Market;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 8 - INITIAL STOP LOSS
  ============================================================ }

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin

   If ( BarsSinceEntry = 0 ) And
      ( SL_Locked = False ) Then Begin
      SL_Line = DC_Lower;
      SL_Trig = SL_Line + ( ATR_Val * SL_ATR_Ratio );
      { v5.3: SL_Pct percentage stop cap (SHORT: ceiling above entry) }
      If SL_Pct > 0 Then
         SL_Trig = MinList( SL_Trig, EntryPrice + ( EntryPrice * SL_Pct / 100 ) );
      SL_Locked = True;
   End;

End Else Begin
   SL_Line   = 0;
   SL_Trig   = 0;
   SL_Locked = False;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 9 - TSL ACTIVATION
  ============================================================ }

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin

   If ( ( Open - Close ) > ( ATR_Val * Accel_M ) ) And
      ( Close < Open ) Then
      Accel = True
   Else
      Accel = False;

   If Close < Lowest( Close[1], NLow_N ) Then
      NLow = True
   Else
      NLow = False;

   If Accel = True And NLow = True Then
      C1_Bar = True
   Else
      C1_Bar = False;

   If ( TSL_Armed = False ) And
      ( C1_Bar    = True  ) And
      ( C1_Bar[1] = True  ) And
      ( BarsSinceEntry >= MinBars ) Then
      TSL_Armed = True;

End Else Begin
   Accel     = False;
   NLow      = False;
   C1_Bar    = False;
   TSL_Armed = False;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 10 - TSL TRACKING
  ============================================================ }

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin

   If TSL_Armed = True Then Begin

      New_TSL = Lowest( Close[1], TSL_K ) +
                ( ATR_Val * TSL_M );

      If TSL_Line = 0 Then
         TSL_Line = New_TSL
      Else
         TSL_Line = MinList( TSL_Line, New_TSL );

      Active_TSL = TSL_Line + ( ATR_Val * SL_ATR_Ratio );

      If TSL_Line < SL_Trig Then
         Active_SL = Active_TSL
      Else
         Active_SL = SL_Trig;

   End Else Begin
      New_TSL    = 0;
      TSL_Line   = 0;
      Active_TSL = 0;
      Active_SL  = SL_Trig;
   End;

End Else Begin
   New_TSL    = 0;
   TSL_Line   = 0;
   Active_TSL = 0;
   Active_SL  = 0;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 11 - TRAILING TAKE PROFIT (TTP)
  ============================================================ }

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin

   If BarsSinceEntry = 0 Then
      LowestClose = Close
   Else
      LowestClose = MinList( LowestClose, Close );

   WaveProfit   = EntryPrice - LowestClose;
   MinProfitPts = ATR_Val * TTP_MinAtr;
   TTP_Line     = LowestClose * ( 1.0 + TTP_RebPct / 100.0 );

   If WaveProfit >= MinProfitPts Then
      TTP_Gate = True
   Else
      TTP_Gate = False;

   If TTP_Gate = True And
      Close > TTP_Line Then
      TTP_Fire = True
   Else
      TTP_Fire = False;

End Else Begin
   LowestClose  = 0;
   WaveProfit   = 0;
   MinProfitPts = 0;
   TTP_Line     = 0;
   TTP_Gate     = False;
   TTP_Fire     = False;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 12 - STOP PROFIT MODULE
  ============================================================ }

If MarketPosition = 0 Then Begin
   posbleProfit_Short = 0;
   stopProfitPrice    = 0;
End;

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin
   If ( EntryPrice - Close ) >= stopProfitPoints_Shrt Then Begin
      If ( EntryPrice - Close ) > posbleProfit_Short Then
         posbleProfit_Short = EntryPrice - Close;
      stopProfitPrice = EntryPrice -
         ( posbleProfit_Short * ( 1.0 - profitReturnPrcnt_Shrt / 100.0 ) );
   End;
End;


{ ============================================================
  SECTION 13 - EXIT CONDITIONS

  LABEL REFERENCE:
    TS_Entry       : short entry signal
    TS_Kill        : manual kill switch (typhoon / emergency)
    TS_RegistryEnd : holiday-registry horizon fail-safe exit
    TS_Holiday     : pre-holiday forced flat (iron rule)
    TS_Settlement  : monthly settlement forced flat (12:30)
    TS_WeeklyExit  : weekly filter forced exit (trend reversal)
    TS_StructureTP : structure reversal take profit
    TS_TTP         : trailing take profit
    TS_StopProfit  : stop profit protection module
    TS_TSL_D       : trailing stop loss day session
    TS_TSL_N       : trailing stop loss night session
    TS_InitSL_D    : initial stop loss day session
    TS_InitSL_N    : initial stop loss night session

  PRIORITY ORDER:
    0. TS_Kill / TS_RegistryEnd / TS_Holiday / TS_Settlement
       (Next Bar at Market)
    1. TS_WeeklyExit   (Next Bar at Market)
    2. TS_StructureTP  (Next Bar at Market)
    3. TS_TTP          (Next Bar at Market)
    4. TS_StopProfit   (Next Bar at Stop)
    5. TS_InitSL_D / TS_TSL_D  (Next Bar at Stop, day)
    6. TS_InitSL_N / TS_TSL_N  (Next Bar at Market, night)
  ============================================================ }

ExitFired = 0;

If MarketPosition = -1 Then Begin

   { Priority 0 - Manual kill / registry fail-safe / holiday iron rule }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And ( Manual_Kill_Switch = True ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_Kill" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And ( v_Registry_Expired = True ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_RegistryEnd" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And ( v_Holiday_Block = True ) And
      ( Time >= Holiday_Flat_Time ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_Holiday" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And ( v_Settlement_Day = True ) And
      ( Time >= Settlement_Flat_Time ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_Settlement" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   { Priority 1 - Weekly filter forced exit }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( DayOfWeek( Date ) = 5 ) And
      ( Time = 1245 ) And
      ( WkBarCount >= WkSMA_Len ) And
      ( Close > ( WkSMASum / WkSMA_Len ) ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_WeeklyExit" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   { Priority 2 - Structure reversal take profit }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( Close > Highest( Close[1], TP_N ) ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_StructureTP" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   { Priority 3 - Trailing take profit }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( TTP_Fire = True ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_TTP" ) Next Bar at Market;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   { Priority 4 - Stop profit }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( stopProfitPrice > 0 ) Then Begin
      BuyToCover( "TS_StopProfit" ) Next Bar at stopProfitPrice Stop;
      ExitFired = 1;
   End;

   { Priority 5 - Day session stop order }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( IsDay = True ) And
      ( Active_SL > 0 ) Then Begin
      If TSL_Armed = True Then
         BuyToCover( "TS_TSL_D" ) Next Bar at Active_SL Stop
      Else
         BuyToCover( "TS_InitSL_D" ) Next Bar at Active_SL Stop;
   End;

   { Priority 6 - Night session close confirmed exit }
   If ( ExitFired = 0 ) And
      ( IsNight = True ) And
      ( Active_SL > 0 ) And
      ( Close > Active_SL ) Then Begin
      If TSL_Armed = True Then
         BuyToCover( "TS_TSL_N" ) Next Bar at Market
      Else
         BuyToCover( "TS_InitSL_N" ) Next Bar at Market;
   End;

End;
